<font color="#993322">

<table align='CENTER' cellpadding='2' border='1' cellspacing='2' background='http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif'><TR><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=10&y=2002">This Month</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=9&y=2002">September-2002</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=8&y=2002">August-2002</A></TD></TR><TR><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=7&y=2002">July-2002</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=6&y=2002">June-2002</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=5&y=2002">May-2002</A></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><CENTER><font size=+2>August, 2002</font><BR></center><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>ToV - HoT Success!</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Saturday - August 31st 2002</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>Ready to test our might against an ancient evil we all headed to Legerdemain's first Halls of Testing raid in the Temple of Veeshan. 
<br>
<br>
Our first pull of the day proved what dangerous place ToV truly is, we all were killed rather quickly due to pets gaining agro before Wuddar. Not willing to accept defeat so easily we prepared our second attack with newly gained knowledge and vigor. 
<br>
<br>
On our next pull everyone ran for cover from the wurms deadly area effect spells while Wuddar stood his ground, not willing to succumb to this menacing wurm. Once the wurm was intent on making Wuddar his next meal we braced ourselves and charged into battle.....
<br>
<br>
Group one was Keymarad, Wuddar (MA), Sweetblithe, Embren, Joredor, Tileren. 
<br>
Group two was Zzeep, Futtal (SA), Xardan, Quila, Gann, Skrambold.
<br>
Group three was Samanthea, Kabniel, Ninden.
<br>
<br>
The wurm fought fiercely but was not prepared for such powerful adversaries. Soon the wurm was dead and we prepared for the rest of our assaults.
<br>
<br>
All I can say is, truly an amazing job everyone. After a few pulls everyone was performing like a ToV pro! I didn't see one mistake, no over nuking, no early assists, nothing, nada, zip! We had a little over two groups and kicked wurm butt big time!
<br>
<table align="center" border=1>
<TR><TD>Samanthea</TD><TD>Unadorned Plate Helm</TD></TR>
<TR><TD>Sweetblithe</TD><TD>Tattered Silk Sleeves</TD></TR>
<TR><TD>Quila</TD><TD>Unadorned Chain Bracelet</TD></TR>
<TR><TD>Wuddar</TD><TD>Unadorned Breastplate</TD></TR>
<TR><TD>Zzeep</TD><TD>Unadorned Gauntlets</TD></TR>
<TR><TD>Tileren</TD><TD>Unadorned Leather Bracelet</TD></TR>
</table>
<br>
Well done everyone!</font><BR><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:drizzt@attglobal.net>Ninden</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>Trak Down, Deyna Loot!</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Sunday - August 25th 2002</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>Wow!!!<BR>
Last time we went up against Trak, we got him down to 50% with some help.  This time, Alasha from Fallen Alliance asked some of her friends to help out.  A large number of FA members showed up to lend a hand! /cheer FA<BR>
We finally got down to Trak, prepared and BOOM! He probably lasted about 30seconds.<BR>
<CENTER>
<img src="http://www.guild-legerdemain.com/memberfiles/user63/trak.jpg" border=0>
</CENTER>
<BR>
He also dropped the Wild Lord Tunic hehehe.  Ahh well.<BR>
Gratz on your epic, Deyna!!</font><BR><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>Renux down!</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Friday - August 16th 2002</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>Friday night Hriyn, Joredor, Zzeep, Kennington, Samanthea, Sweetblithe, Bubben, and yours truly assembled a force and headed for Steamfont Mountains intent on taking out Renux Herkanor. 
<BR>
<BR>
Our plan was simple. Once we all were buffed and ready Bubben was to kit Renux around while everyone else smacked her around. Bubben performed an excellent pull once Renux was spawned. After a few rounds of nimble kiting Renux saw and opening in Bubbens defenses and hit with deadly precision. Seeing our valiant druid in peril Samanthea unleashed her healing powers, but alas the swift blades were tainted with a deadly poison...
<BR>
<BR>
Renux filled with anger and struck out at Samanthea to claim yet another victim. The attacks were relentless and quick. Seeing the fall of their comrades Joredor and Sweetblithe went into action casting with all their might to gain the attention of Renux. Good and evil magic combined together left Renux enraged to the point of confusion. Filled with rage, inspired with the deaths of their two friends, Hriyn and Ninden took this opportunity to unleashed a flurry of blades. Zzeep and Kennington were there to aid in our attack using their healing powers to assure Renux shall not claim another life again.
<BR>
<BR>
After a short while our force accomplished what they set out to do.....
<BR>
Renux is no more.
<BR>
<BR>
<BR>
Grats Hriyn on your epic pieces! 
<BR>
Loot dropped:
Jagged Diamond Dagger, Translated Parchment, Trochilc's Skean, Ravenscale Neckguard, and Ravenscale Mask.

</font><BR><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:drizzt@attglobal.net>Ninden</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>Faydoodoo down, Tileren lewt!</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Saturday - August 10th 2002</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>Yay! After one failure, Fay has fallen to Legerd for the first time as a guild.  Thank you Cackling, Koldwind, Woundless, Helmm, and Gotenn for adding to our party.  Now Tileren has a leafblower heheh.<BR>
Way to go, everyone!</font><BR><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>Holy Flying Turd, Batman!</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Monday - August 5th 2002</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>O...M... G... Gann got his epic!!!!<BR>
You should congratulate Gann when next you get a chance.  He's the most recently epic Legerdemain member.  Not to say that any epic is "easy", but the mage epic is quite difficult.  It's taken a boatload of time and dedication on Gann's part and a lot of help from his friends.  He really deserves a big pat on the back :><BR>
<BR>
Gann  ist  uuber!</font><BR><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>Hate for Gann!</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Thursday - August 1st 2002</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>Posted by Gann:<BR>
Well we had quite a fun day in hate yesterday. The start was a bit slow, we had to wait 20 minutes for a main assist and puller, but after that it was smooth sailing... Well, truthfully there were a few minor bumps. We had a rough break in with few people making to the SS. Luckily for us however skrambold and keymarad both made it. ( I never think we really appreciated how good ninden was at CR until he wasn't there.) I was impressed by peoples patience and understanding during the first half of the raid. After we cleaned up that whole mess and got moving again the rest of the night went awesome. We had excellent CC *props to Embren and Qildadar* along with everyones cooperation on assist commands.<BR>
<BR>
We were lucky to find our target mob Magi P'tasa wielding his staff. ( We promptly kicked his butt and took it, completing my epic! Yay me.) After that we asked if everyone wanted to stay. Everyone seemed interested and so we moved to the throne room for evening. We killed many demi gods and picked up some nice loot. It was a good fun experience for everyone I believe especially a few first time Hate raiders.<BR>
<BR>
I'd personally like to thank everyone in the guild for their support in my epic battles, you were always there when I needed you. I need to turn in some stuff still, but i hope to have my orb in the next few days. Also thanks for your patience during the rough times, without your understanding none of this would have been possible.<BR>
<BR>
Without further ado and spam: THE DROPS!!!<BR>
